  ('ff804b31-4f57-479f-b421-21ed92d8c047','Diamond Archery LLC in Wichita, Kansas runs a solidly equipped commercial operation, with a 16-lane range, an on-site pro shop, and formal lessons available for archers just getting started. That combination covers a lot of ground for one shop, letting a beginner take a lesson, then move to lane time, with a pro shop on hand for equipment needs in between. Wichita''s size as Kansas''s largest city supports a real market for a commercial range with this level of program depth, drawing archers and hunters from across the metro area. Anyone interested in lessons or general range access should contact Diamond Archery directly.'),
  ('90322421-73bf-4fa4-93c1-85d3a7da495a','Double G Archery in Georgetown, Texas operates as a commercial range with an on-site pro shop, useful for archers who need arrows fletched, a bow tuned, or new gear without driving into Austin. Lessons are offered too, making it a reasonable starting point for someone picking up a bow for the first time or working on form with an instructor rather than guessing alone. Georgetown''s growth has brought a steady stream of new residents looking for local activities, and a commercial range with instruction fills that niche well. Beyond the pro shop and lessons, Double G Archery''s own listings or a phone call will have the specifics on lanes, distances, and open hours.'),
  ('1f42a339-f59e-4d58-a416-b87e4a30fa47','Double T Archery is a club-style range in Amherst, New York, part of the Buffalo suburbs'' small but committed archery scene. Clubs like this one tend to run on member involvement rather than storefront hours, so the day-to-day experience depends heavily on who''s shooting and when. Western New York''s archery community leans toward bowhunting prep through the fall and target practice the rest of the year, and a club setup usually means a more social, lower-key atmosphere than a commercial range. There''s no confirmed detail here on programs, lane counts, or a pro shop, so anyone interested in shooting at Double T Archery should reach out to the club directly for membership terms and access.'),
  ('18c06058-a15d-4989-aca1-4019bb595cd9','Douglas Archery serves Ogden, Utah as a commercial range with a pro shop on-site, giving local archers a place to buy arrows, get equipment serviced, or just talk shop between rounds. Ogden sits close to the Wasatch foothills, an area with a strong bowhunting tradition, and a pro shop in town is a convenient stop before or after scouting trips into the mountains. As a walk-in commercial operation, Douglas Archery doesn''t require a membership commitment the way a club would. No lesson programs, 3D course, or field course are listed for this location, so archers wanting those specifics, along with lane count and hours, should check with Douglas Archery directly.'),
  ('54f4bfb1-ae10-462d-a251-a7c28544e51b','Dover Consolidated Sportsmen is a club in Dover, New Jersey, part of the sportsmen''s club tradition common across the state, where archery often shares grounds with fishing, trapping, or hunting-focused activities. Morris County has a long history of these multi-purpose sportsmen''s organizations, and a club-based range typically means scheduled shoot times and membership dues rather than drop-in access. There''s nothing on record here about lesson programs, a 3D course, or a pro shop at this location, so it likely operates on a smaller, member-driven scale. Archers interested in joining should contact Dover Consolidated Sportsmen directly to ask about membership requirements, guest policies, and when the range is actually open to shoot.'),
  ('bd443853-61bc-476b-ac76-20c846d8c272','Dreamcatcher Archery is a commercial range in Las Vegas, Nevada, a city where extreme summer heat shapes a lot of outdoor recreation timing. As a walk-in commercial operation, it doesn''t carry the membership structure of a club, so archers can generally show up and shoot without joining anything first. Nothing is confirmed here about a pro shop, lesson program, or course type at this location, so the range''s exact setup isn''t detailed in the available data. Anyone in the Las Vegas valley curious about Dreamcatcher Archery should call ahead or check its listings directly to confirm hours, pricing, and what the range actually offers before visiting.'),
  ('d864c9e7-db16-47ec-96a8-2257c04474f8','Drop Tine Archery operates as a commercial range in Charlotte, North Carolina, one of a handful of walk-in archery options serving the fast-growing Charlotte metro. A commercial setup like this typically means no membership requirement, just pay-to-shoot access for locals and visitors alike. Charlotte''s suburbs have absorbed a lot of new residents in recent years, many coming from areas with less hunting and shooting culture, so a commercial range can serve as an easy entry point for someone trying archery for the first time. There''s no confirmed information here on a pro shop, lessons, or course type at Drop Tine Archery, so anyone planning a visit should contact the range directly to confirm current hours, pricing, and what''s actually available on site.'),
  ('5fb1c988-4444-46a7-9273-d9ef74775b41','Dropshot Archery brings a commercial range with both a pro shop and lesson programs to Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, a city where dedicated archery space is genuinely hard to come by. Having equipment sales and service on-site alongside instruction means someone can walk in without any gear, take a lesson, and leave having actually tried the sport, rather than needing to source a bow elsewhere first. That combination is particularly useful in a dense urban market where most residents don''t have a home range or family history with the sport. Specific lane counts, distances, and hours aren''t listed here, so Philadelphia archers interested in Dropshot Archery should reach out directly to check current scheduling and pricing before showing up.'),
  ('4fa0ea75-c8b9-4e6e-9e54-7d681ee4d393','Dulce Jicarilla Bowhunters Archery Club is based in Dulce, New Mexico, seat of the Jicarilla Apache Nation in the northern part of the state. Bowhunting has deep cultural roots across the region, and a club carrying that name signals a group organized specifically around hunting-oriented archery rather than Olympic-style target shooting. As a club, it likely runs on a membership or community basis rather than public walk-in hours, and no programs, course type, or pro shop are confirmed for this listing. Dulce sits in a remote, high-country part of New Mexico near the Colorado border, so local archers depend on clubs like this one for organized shooting rather than commercial alternatives. Contact the club directly for membership details and access.')
